## 1. The probe's CONTRACT (header), replacing the class-L closure claim

Backup first: `mvme187_memc_probe.py.pre_r6` (cmp-identical to the in-tree probe before the edit AND to
r5_20261105/table5/probe206_frozen.py; md5 5d0cb614dc185067ee850d975a904062, the one T5_PREP.md:12 records).

**REPAIR 5 paragraph (probe :29-36 before, :29-41 after).**  Replaced.  Before (the closure claim): "R16 ... and R17 ... drive
every access kind (arm x direction x controller, byte stores of 0x00 and 0xff, word stores of 0xffffffff) in every phase and read
both latches (a memconf store, a default access) and the three served fields after each; R5, R7, R9, R12, R13 and R15 gain tails
that repeat each notice category after its first access (a second memconf store after first stores of 0x00, 0x07, 0xff,
0xffffffff; a second default access after first reads at 0x0c, 0x7c, 0xff, 0xf3 and first writes at 0x18, 0xe7, 0x1c, 0x118)".
After: what R16, R17 and the six tails actually do, each clause checked against the instruction lists (R16 :527-541, R17 :576-582,
tails: R5 :318-321, R7 :351-353, R9 :381-383, R12 :445-451, R13 :475-477, R15 :507-509), then the R1 sentence: the rows are
COVERAGE; no controller-0 memconf store occurs in phase 10 (R16's is ST_B(0,3,0x108), controller 1), no controller-1 default
store in phase 11, no chipid/chiprev readback after R16's phase-11 tail.  (The old "second default access after first reads at
0x7c, 0xff, 0xf3 and first writes at 0x18, 0xe7, 0x1c" was also false: R3's, R11's and R17's first reads and R5's, R14's and
R15's first writes are not followed by a second default access in the tails -- replaced by the true list.)

**CONTRACT paragraph (new, probe :43-79; clause (e) now :81-133 -- after the rec7 edit, section 6: CONTRACT :43-89, clause (e) :91-143; after the rec8 edit, section 7: CONTRACT :43-88, clause (e) :90-142).**  The ruling's section-2 text, checked clause by clause against PRETABLE_5.out's
survivor summary (:9460-9697) and against the function (dev_mvme187.c:59-144), and TIGHTENED in four places where the ruling's
wording was wrong or incomplete -- each as hard a check as pass 4 got:
  (a) The ruling's COVERED clause "any kept store into any served field ungated or gated on direction or controller alone" is
      FALSE for two of its own disclosed families: NB3 is a keep gated on controller alone (PRETABLE_5.out:9616 `UNOBSERVED MB C`)
      and NB4 is `&=` gated on !controller alone (:8199, :8211 equivalents).  The contract now says "except the cells disclosed
      below" and lists them.
  (b) The ruling's section-2 list (2) dropped "a latch written from an arm that does not read it", which its own section 1(b)(ii)
      disclosed; restored (it covers L_DT_M_idat under nC.D at :9600 and L_CI/L_CR_*_xor1 under W.nC at :9525, :9546).
  (c) The ruling's "(1 ^ v stays true)" is false for v = 1 (`^= 1` on a set latch clears it and is red).  Qualified: truthy for
      every store value the rows use (0x05, 0x07, 0x5a, 0xff, 0xffffffff).
  (d) One UNOBSERVED group the ruling's section 1(b) enumeration (i)-(iv) does not cover: `d->warned_memconf = idata` at the
      memconf arm's end under `writeflag == MEM_WRITE && !controller` (:9637 `ME W.nC`, :9639 `ME W.nC.M`, L_ME_M_idat; NOT
      `!controller` alone -- ME lies after the write block, reads have idata 0, and L_ME_M_idat_nC is red 201/206 at SCORES.txt:570
      while L_ME_M_idat_W.nC is green at :2999: rec6 F2, section 6).  It is the fix's OWN latch under
      the arm's own direction test plus controller; it survives because every controller-0 0x00 memconf store (R3's second, R7's
      second, R9's third) is the last memconf store of its session.  Verified by walking all eleven multi-access sessions'
      memconf stores.  Outside the floor by the ruling's own rule (controller is not a floor predicate), so DEBT: disclosed under
      (2), filed (FILING item 2(vi)), closed by the same remedy as family (1).
  Also made explicit: the toggles whose only odd driver is R10's 0x5a (DA/DT/H/TL under ib0c/ib2c/ib5c/ib7c, :9571-9574,
  :9596-9599, :9612-9613, :9686-9689) -- the ruling's (b)(iii) names them but its section-2 disclosure (4) did not.
  Every other survivor-summary line was placed under one of the disclosures (1)-(5) or the closing "Also disclosed" sentences
  (since rec7 split into WALKED BUT NOT CLOSED -- the supplementary alphabet and the cross-call caveat -- and NOT WALKED; the
  records-6 text called all of it "outside the walk", which was false for the idata-bit-8..31 gates and the VACUOUS cells, both
  walked: PRETABLE_5.out:18-20, memc_variants_5.py:791-795; rec6 F1); none was left unclassified.

**CLAUSE (e) lead-in (probe :38-41 before).**  Before: "CLAUSE (e) -- catches (test-variant table 4, ... all 112 of 112 variants
red on this 148-row probe)".  After: table 5 named as the record with its numbers (3,575 = 112 + 3,463; 2,798 red
representatives for 26,999 predicted-red cells; 665 green, all predicted, all in disclosed families; every table-4 variant red
