## 3. PROOF that the probe edit is text-only

Command (from GXEMUL-SEC/regress/):

    python -I artifacts/mvme187memcoob/r6_20261105/textonly_check.py mvme187_memc_probe.py \
        artifacts/mvme187memcoob/r5_20261105/table5/probe206_frozen.py

Result of the records-6 run (kept in `TEXTONLY_PROOF.txt.pre_rec7`):

    check 1 (ast.dump, module docstring dropped, every string constant -> 'S'): EQUAL
       dump length edited=117162 frozen=117162
    check 2 (string constants in source order): edited=836 frozen=836
       differs: edited :313 (note) 'ld.bu +0x7c (first byte past memcreg: the first latch byte)' <- frozen :265 'ld.bu +0x7c (first byte past the struct)'
       differs: edited :332 (note) 'the load past memcreg (the first latch byte) reads 0' <- frozen :284 'the past-struct load reads 0'
       differs: edited :420 (note) '+0x%x reads 0: no struct byte forwarded' <- frozen :371 '+0x%x reads 0: no image byte forwarded'
       3 string constants differ; all notes: yes
    TEXTONLY_CHECK=PASS

Result of the rec7 re-run, after section 6's header edit (saved verbatim in `TEXTONLY_PROOF.txt`; the same three notes, ten lines
further down because the module docstring grew by ten lines, 658 -> 668; exit 0, 0 CR bytes, `ast.parse` ok):

    check 1 (ast.dump, module docstring dropped, every string constant -> 'S'): EQUAL
       dump length edited=117162 frozen=117162
    check 2 (string constants in source order): edited=836 frozen=836
       differs: edited :323 (note) 'ld.bu +0x7c (first byte past memcreg: the first latch byte)' <- frozen :265 'ld.bu +0x7c (first byte past the struct)'
       differs: edited :342 (note) 'the load past memcreg (the first latch byte) reads 0' <- frozen :284 'the past-struct load reads 0'
       differs: edited :430 (note) '+0x%x reads 0: no struct byte forwarded' <- frozen :371 '+0x%x reads 0: no image byte forwarded'
       3 string constants differ; all notes: yes
    TEXTONLY_CHECK=PASS

Check 1 is the round's criterion: with the module docstring dropped and every string constant replaced by a placeholder, the two
ASTs dump identically, so no instruction word, seed, want, register list, control flag or sentinel changed.  Check 2 is the
supplement check 1 cannot give (row names and `has()` fragments are string literals too, and they are logic): exactly three
string constants differ, each the `note` of a row (the `rd 0x7c` note reaches row() through the loop variable at :317).
Row names, notice fragments, format strings and sentinels are unchanged.  The first version of the script reported "0 string
constants differ" -- a false pass caused by placeholdering the tree in place before listing it -- and was caught because three
notes were known to differ; the script's comment records that.  `python -I -c "ast.parse(...)"` also parses the edited probe;
line endings stay LF (0 CR bytes); the full edit is `mvme187_memc_probe.py.r6.diff` (diff -u against the backup).

